(10) The grant of such license will not cause a violation of this article or any other ordinance or regulation of DeKalb County, the State of Georgia, or the United States;
(11) No individual having an interest either as an owner, partner, principal stockholder, directly or indirectly beneficial or absolute, is in violation of section 15-410 of this Code;
(12) The applicant is not overdue on payment to the county on taxes, fees, fines, or penalties assessed against, or imposed on the applicant; and
(13) The applicant is not residing with or married to a person (i) who has been denied an adult entertainment license within twelve (12) months immediately preceding the date of the application, (ii) whose adult entertainment license has been revoked within twelve (12) months immediately preceding the date of the application, or (iii) whose adult entertainment establishment license is under suspension at the time of the application.
